<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex (gpt-6-astra), independent Tibetan-first proposal; no hgm_gloss promotion. GMR English is preserved verbatim. The tshad mar song ba constructions are aligned as evaluative phrases, not artificial lexical song ba equivalents. The two source appearances in each relevant construction supply looked-like and appeared/appearing roles; the single final tsam attaches to the first hell-object clause, while GMR's repeated descriptive expansions remain unwrapped. The snang-gzhi clause retains its actual-object role. Med supplies the negative of couldn't by the established n't convention. Lha yi is retained without a source correction; its local English recipient recast is recorded only at lha. Mechanical fidelity is not semantic approval.</div>
